{"id": "EUVD-2026-76564", "enisaUuid": "b6238df9-679c-3499-834d-2c0130517798", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nceph: bound copied dentry name length in NFS export get_name\n\nceph_get_name() copies the MDS-supplied name into the caller's\nNAME_MAX-sized buffer with memcpy(name, rinfo->dname, rinfo->dname_len)\nand then writes name[rinfo->dname_len] = 0, without checking dname_len\nagainst NAME_MAX. A malicious or buggy MDS that returns a LOOKUPNAME reply\nwith dname_len > NAME_MAX overflows the buffer. __get_snap_name() copies\nrde->name / rde->name_len the same unchecked way.\n\nImpact: a malicious or compromised Ceph MDS overflows the NAME_MAX name\nbuffer in a client's NFS-export get_name path, a slab out-of-bounds write\nreported by KASAN. Reachable when a CephFS mount is re-exported over NFS.\n\nAdd ceph_export_copy_name(), which rejects lengths above NAME_MAX with\n-ENAMETOOLONG before the copy, and use it in both ceph_get_name() and\n__get_snap_name().", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:45:42", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:50:23", "baseScore": 9.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a294064e0e0f81ea607b2f019e16888aa1b0a011", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/61d9f27b191b838b96b697ce0bfaee39a138243a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/06fb5e623cdc2402d6bb29be94d9beb9a826ffec", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e7c2fd3893a7f7fcd7e8cf0b2c6348bb1e893df6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/eff8013c5a8916613c742ae5a2cc341cb605c0ae"], "aliases": ["GHSA-rgf4-v7fw-49xj", "CVE-2026-89652"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.46, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "11fd87f2-4e97-342f-9aa6-6cd157d4b3a3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.109"}, {"id": "1e2e12b9-ba67-3594-bedc-0ff99f1075c3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "19913b4eac4a230dccb548931358398f45dabe4c <e7c2fd3893a7f7fcd7e8cf0b2c6348bb1e893df6"}, {"id": "34bbb445-a86d-3009-888a-1713d16b6f0e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "19913b4eac4a230dccb548931358398f45dabe4c <06fb5e623cdc2402d6bb29be94d9beb9a826ffec"}, {"id": "48ffc3ce-244a-3006-959f-2ee519845317", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "19913b4eac4a230dccb548931358398f45dabe4c <eff8013c5a8916613c742ae5a2cc341cb605c0ae"}, {"id": "4e79455c-e747-356e-af6f-664789ee14f8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "51445ced-5373-3ccf-a585-79536ebb8214", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.50"}, {"id": "89665e2e-19f8-3f88-8eb3-f08f6a25194f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "19913b4eac4a230dccb548931358398f45dabe4c <a294064e0e0f81ea607b2f019e16888aa1b0a011"}, {"id": "9004d28a-d456-3f69-bee2-2a7c8b5feb1b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.157"}, {"id": "96303330-26e4-3cb2-b441-e7a252fef90c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.4"}, {"id": "ac85f6e0-54cb-3b60-80ea-efc53b027f27", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "b21aa847-b705-3e49-ab80-ee50de1a44c5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3.15"}, {"id": "e3d278ef-81f0-3bb6-9c31-01fc9d2ee0c2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "19913b4eac4a230dccb548931358398f45dabe4c <61d9f27b191b838b96b697ce0bfaee39a138243a"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "0a3f6d7f-5a9d-3056-b0b0-d9aaffd5744a", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}